{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310942,"nonce":"j/LqhFmQblhodi5F5L/RROkao3A=","title":"A native of xwindow.wasm called from a Haxe thread throws, where blinc_abi's works (after a1e4499a)","message":"After 89386eb was fixed, a thread can call blinc_abi.wasm's primitives. A primitive of xwindow.wasm called from a thread throws a `haxe.ValueException` with an empty message, in a page and under `ash run`; the same call on the main thread returns.\n\n**Reproducer**\n\nblinc_abi.wasm, xgpu.wasm and xwindow.wasm beside the program, built with `ASH_WASM_FIBERS=1 ash --build probe.wasm --target wasm32-wasip1-threads probe.hl`:\n\n    class ThreadWake {\n        static function main() {\n            try {\n                Sys.println(\"main: wake = \" + window.Window.wake());      // main: wake = false\n            } catch (e:haxe.Exception) { Sys.println('main failed: ${e.message}'); }\n            var lock = new sys.thread.Lock();\n            sys.thread.Thread.create(() -\u003e {\n                try {\n                    Sys.println(\"thread: wake = \" + window.Window.wake());\n                } catch (e:haxe.Exception) {\n                    Sys.println('thread failed: [${e.message}]');         // thread failed: []\n                }\n                lock.release();\n            });\n            Sys.println(lock.wait(5) ? \"joined\" : \"timeout\");\n        }\n    }\n\n`window.Window.wake` is `@:hlNative(\"xwindow\", \"window_wake\")`; the web build of the primitive does nothing and returns false. The same shape with `Bitmap.fromBytes` (blinc_abi) works in a thread.\n\n**Why it matters**\n\nashui's `Work.notify`, called when a thread queues UI work, calls the window's `wake` from the thread. ashui's `Worker.run` does it after every job (textures compressed, skies built), so the first job's result handing kills the program: \"uncaught exception: instance of haxe.ValueException\", \"hlp_throw called without active trap; aborting\", trap `unreachable`. The banner scene in a page hits it on its first texture.\n\n**Possibly**\n\nOnly the first library's functions, or only the libraries a thread has already called into before, are bound in a thread's instance; or a lookup of a name not yet resolved on the main thread fails.","files":null}]}